{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'licenses|Library licenses|case.licenses' src/ui.js build.mjs src/template.html && rg -n 'setAnimationLoop|isWebGPUBackend' node_modules/three/src/renderers/common/Renderer.js | head -n 12 && du -sh . node_modules\"","aggregated_output":"build.mjs:9:const licenses = await readFile('THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt','utf8');\nbuild.mjs:11:template=template.replace('/*HUB_CLIENT*/',()=>session).replace('/*GAME_STYLE*/',()=>css).replace('/*METADATA*/',()=>JSON.stringify(interview).replaceAll('<','\\\\u003c')).replace('/*LICENSES*/',()=>JSO [... omitted end of long line]\nsrc/ui.js:20: about(){const m=window.GAME_META;const grid=Object.entries(m.sourceInformation).map(([k,v])=>'<dt>'+k.replace(/([A-Z])/g,' $1').replace(/^./,c=>c.toUpperCase())+'</dt><dd>'+escape(v)+'</dd>').join('' [... omitted end of long line]\nsrc/ui.js:22: show(screen,preserve=false){const g=this.g;if(!preserve){if(['help','settings','about','network'].includes(screen)&&!['help','settings','about','network'].includes(g.screen))this.origin=g.screen==='n [... omitted end of long line]\nsrc/ui.js:34: async action(a){const g=this.g;if(!a)return;if(a.startsWith('setting:')){const key=a.slice(8);if(key==='glyphs')g.settings.glyphs=g.settings.glyphs==='ps'?'xbox':'ps';else if(key==='camera')g.setting [... omitted end of long line]\n1620:\tasync setAnimationLoop( callback ) {\n1624:\t\tthis._animation.setAnimationLoop( callback );\n2215:\t\tthis.setAnimationLoop( null );\n58M\t.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('src/game.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"if(e.code==='ArrowDown'||e.code==='KeyS')this.ui.move(1);\\\", \\\"if(e.code==='Tab')this.ui.move(e.shiftKey?-1:1);else if(e.code==='ArrowDown'||e.code==='KeyS')this.ui.move(1);\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/ui.js');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace(\\\"\"'!['\"'help','settings','about','network'].includes(g.screen)\\\",\\\"['title','pause','result','none'].includes(g.screen)\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"elements.forEach((el,i)=>{el.addEventListener('pointerenter'\\\", \\\"elements.forEach((el,i)=>{el.addEventListener('focus',()=>{this.focusIndex=i;for(const other of elements)other.classList.toggle('focused',other===el);});el.addEventListener('pointerenter'\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/style.css');s=p.read_text()+'''\\\\n.status-line>span{font-size:.72rem;min-width:5rem}.status-line b{font-size:.95rem}#actionHints{font-size:.78rem}#actionHints .glyph{font-size:.8rem;height:1.7rem;min-width:1.7rem}#speedLine{font-size:.65rem}body.touch .status-line>span{font-size:.6rem;min-width:4.2rem}body.touch .status-line b{font-size:.75rem}\\\\n''';p.write_text(s)\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Chromium 153; WebGPU and WebGL 2; scripted complete mission and attract replay, emulated standard gamepad, simultaneous touch at 844×390, live/offline audio signals, two-page BroadcastChannel and WebRTC, and the official AI Hub harness with 2/4 players, 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss and host departure. Physical-device/listening review unknown.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n'Testing caught 6 issues: inline-script packaging corruption, reversed craft face winding, Enter launching immediately after leaving attract mode, twin cannon rays missing the aim point, stale victory state on restart, and a tow camera that cropped the walker. All were fixed.',\n'2 critical issues: the initial startup packaging error and unreliable cannon convergence. Both were fixed.',\n'The complete AI playthrough and independent attract-mode playthrough: they exercise real Rapier projectile hits, both cable takedowns, escort progression, the ace, victory, and the replay loop.',\n'Headless WebGPU screenshots were blank on this machine. State checks verified WebGPU, and WebGL screenshots supplied the visual review.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n'Three.js makes procedural geometry, banded toon shading, native transform animation and multiple camera styles straightforward. WebGPURenderer also supplies a useful WebGL 2 backend.',\n'I initially reversed the custom wedge mesh winding and aimed parallel twin-gun rays beside the target. Visual review and actual Rapier hit tests exposed these assumptions; both were corrected.',\n'The arcade flight model, guided tow orbit and tension mechanic, data-driven mission, controller menu focus, synthesized audio and ghost-rival transports.',\n'Coordinating WebGPU initialization and headless visual capture while keeping physics, animation, input and multiplayer lifecycles consistent.',\n'none',\n'A documented, reliable headless screenshot path across WebGPU adapters and fallback backends.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n'The specific source, cel-shaded direction, controller-first UX, attract mode and complete-demo requirements provided a clear identity and useful acceptance criteria.',\n'The source title also names the film, while 1982 identifies the original video game. I used the snow-battle arcade game as the mechanical anchor and the film for tone.',\n'Making cable takedowns readable and satisfying across controller, mouse and simultaneous touch while delivering all mission stages and multiplayer paths.',\n'Specify whether standalone multiplayer must cross NAT without manual signaling, and whether a WebGL fallback is desired.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('test.py');s=p.read_text();needle=\\\"        # Cooldown, flight handling, damage, failure and pickup systems.\\\"\ns=s.replace(needle,\\\"\\\"\\\"        page.get_by_role('button', name='About & credits').click()\n        credits = page.locator('#menu').inner_text()\n        check('Credits contain source and all feedback sections', all(title in credits for title in ['Source Information','Testing Feedback','Engine Feedback','Prompt Feedback','added on import']))\n        page.get_by_role('button', name='Library licenses').click()\n        check('Third-party licenses included', 'THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED' in page.locator('#menu').inner_text() and 'Apache License' in page.locator('#menu').inner_text())\n        page.get_by_role('button', name='Back to credits').click()\n        page.get_by_role('button', name='Back', exact=True).click()\n        check('Credits and licenses return to result screen', js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().screen') == 'result')\n        # Cooldown, flight handling, damage, failure and pickup systems.\\\"\\\"\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"check('Transport loss ends the sortie', js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().completed && \"'!__POSE__.game.won'\"'))\\\", \\\"check('Transport loss ends the sortie', js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().completed && \"'!__POSE__.game.won'\"'))\\\\n        js(page, '__POSE__.game.begin()')\\\\n        check('Fresh run clears prior victory and result state', not js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().won') and not js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().completed'))\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nbiome check --write --linter-enabled=false --assist-enabled=false src/*.js build.mjs\nbiome format --write src/style.css\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# The Empire Strikes a Pose\n\nAn original, unofficial snow-battle flight comic inspired by the 1982 game. Three.js r180, WebGPU, Rapier 0.19.3. All art, animation, music, effects and gibberish voices are procedural. The root HTML embeds every runtime dependency and can be opened directly with \"'`file://`.\n\nThe deliverable is `../The-Empire-Strikes-a-Pose-Star-Wars-The-Empire-Strikes-Back-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-011138.html`. The exit interview is beside it and is also embedded into About & credits.\n\n## Play\n\nClear three scouts, use tow lines to topple two walkers, then escort Ark and defeat Blackfin. Keep within 145 metres of the transport. A full AI sortie takes about two minutes; a first human sortie is expected to take longer (human timing unknown).\n\n- Keyboard/mouse: WASD steer and throttle, mouse aims, left click fires, Shift boosts, S brakes, Space launches/releases a cable, Q changes target, C changes camera, Escape pauses. J also fires.\n- Standard gamepad: left stick steers and throttles; right stick aims; R2/RT fires; L2/LT boosts; R1/RB brakes; Cross/A tows; Square/X changes target; Triangle/Y changes camera; Options/Menu pauses. D-pad or stick navigates menus, Cross/A selects and Circle/B returns. Xbox labels are available in Settings.\n- Touch: invisible left drag steers/throttles; right drag aims/fires. Cannons assist automatically. A context-sensitive tow button appears beside walkers. Multitouch is supported.\n\nContinuous fire overheats the cannons. Cyan repair buoys restore hull and cool the weapons. While tethered, steer to change orbit radius; boost adds speed and tension. Two wraps topple a walker. The camera widens during cable flight.\n\nPause → Developer tools exposes live speed, turn rate, weapon damage, incoming damage, enemy pressure, wraps and simulation rate; plus reset, invulnerability, AI pilot, collision shapes, repair, frame step, spawn and chapter tools.\n\nTitle idle for ten seconds starts a looping, invulnerable AI demo. Any input returns to the title without launching a run.\n\n## Multiplayer\n\nAI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1–4 seats. Each player has their own world and competes by sortie score. Wing craft are visible in the same mission chapter but cannot collide. The unmodified session client is embedded first in the head. Session startup, seeding, progress, ghost state, time-up result, leave and end behavior follow the supplied contract.\n\nStandalone has same-origin BroadcastChannel rooms for up to four pilots, and a two-player serverless WebRTC invite/answer exchange. The direct link uses host ICE candidates without a public signaling or relay service; use a same-network or directly reachable connection. Internet NAT traversal is unknown. AI Hub manages internet sessions. The Wing link screen includes complete pairing instructions and error messages.\n\n## Build and test\n\nFrom this directory:\n\n```sh\nnpm install --ignore-scripts\nnpm run build\nnpm run --silent test\n```\n\nThe test command prints only failures and one count. It uses the installed Python Playwright environment and Chromium, starts its own loopback HTTP server on an OS-assigned port, verifies the served game identity, closes its own pages/browser and stops its own server. It saves JSON reports and visual-only captures in `test-artifacts/`.\n\nThe suite covers direct-file startup, embedded script parsing, versions, full combat/tow/escort/ace victory, heat, repair, failures, pause and live balance tools, gamepad stubs, touch contacts, attract looping, live/offline audio, both standalone transports, and the official Hub harness in normal, loss/jitter and host-departure cases. WebGPU canvas capture is blank in this headless setup; visual captures use the engine'\"'s WebGL backend. Actual hardware/controller/touch/TV and audible listening review remain unknown.\n\n\"'`?test=1` exposes deterministic simulation hooks on `window.__POSE__`; the normal page exposes only state and audio diagnostics. `?renderer=webgl` explicitly selects the built-in fallback. `?manual=1` disables the animation clock for test driving.\n\n## Extend the slice\n\n`src/mission.js` contains chapter titles, briefing lines, spawn positions, repair placements and default balance. `src/art.js` builds the world and animated machines. `src/game.js` owns simulation, physics and progression; `src/ui.js`, `src/audio.js` and `src/network.js` handle their respective systems. `build.mjs` embeds all code, metadata and third-party license texts into the root HTML. The original Hub client and harness are retained beside the sources.\n\nSource research: none. The explicitly requested AI Hub contract/client/harness and pinned package dependencies were downloaded without web searching. The random title draw used Python `secrets.randbelow(50)`; its result is recorded in `title-selection.json`.\nEOF\nnpm run build\nnpm run --silent test'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('src/game.js');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"if(e.code==='ArrowDown'||e.code==='KeyS')this.ui.move(1);\\\", \\\"if(e.code==='Tab')this.ui.move(e.shiftKey?-1:1);else if(e.code==='ArrowDown'||e.code==='KeyS')this.ui.move(1);\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/ui.js');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace(\\\"\"'!['\"'help','settings','about','network'].includes(g.screen)\\\",\\\"['title','pause','result','none'].includes(g.screen)\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"elements.forEach((el,i)=>{el.addEventListener('pointerenter'\\\", \\\"elements.forEach((el,i)=>{el.addEventListener('focus',()=>{this.focusIndex=i;for(const other of elements)other.classList.toggle('focused',other===el);});el.addEventListener('pointerenter'\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/style.css');s=p.read_text()+'''\\\\n.status-line>span{font-size:.72rem;min-width:5rem}.status-line b{font-size:.95rem}#actionHints{font-size:.78rem}#actionHints .glyph{font-size:.8rem;height:1.7rem;min-width:1.7rem}#speedLine{font-size:.65rem}body.touch .status-line>span{font-size:.6rem;min-width:4.2rem}body.touch .status-line b{font-size:.75rem}\\\\n''';p.write_text(s)\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Chromium 153; WebGPU and WebGL 2; scripted complete mission and attract replay, emulated standard gamepad, simultaneous touch at 844×390, live/offline audio signals, two-page BroadcastChannel and WebRTC, and the official AI Hub harness with 2/4 players, 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss and host departure. Physical-device/listening review unknown.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n'Testing caught 6 issues: inline-script packaging corruption, reversed craft face winding, Enter launching immediately after leaving attract mode, twin cannon rays missing the aim point, stale victory state on restart, and a tow camera that cropped the walker. All were fixed.',\n'2 critical issues: the initial startup packaging error and unreliable cannon convergence. Both were fixed.',\n'The complete AI playthrough and independent attract-mode playthrough: they exercise real Rapier projectile hits, both cable takedowns, escort progression, the ace, victory, and the replay loop.',\n'Headless WebGPU screenshots were blank on this machine. State checks verified WebGPU, and WebGL screenshots supplied the visual review.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n'Three.js makes procedural geometry, banded toon shading, native transform animation and multiple camera styles straightforward. WebGPURenderer also supplies a useful WebGL 2 backend.',\n'I initially reversed the custom wedge mesh winding and aimed parallel twin-gun rays beside the target. Visual review and actual Rapier hit tests exposed these assumptions; both were corrected.',\n'The arcade flight model, guided tow orbit and tension mechanic, data-driven mission, controller menu focus, synthesized audio and ghost-rival transports.',\n'Coordinating WebGPU initialization and headless visual capture while keeping physics, animation, input and multiplayer lifecycles consistent.',\n'none',\n'A documented, reliable headless screenshot path across WebGPU adapters and fallback backends.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n'The specific source, cel-shaded direction, controller-first UX, attract mode and complete-demo requirements provided a clear identity and useful acceptance criteria.',\n'The source title also names the film, while 1982 identifies the original video game. I used the snow-battle arcade game as the mechanical anchor and the film for tone.',\n'Making cable takedowns readable and satisfying across controller, mouse and simultaneous touch while delivering all mission stages and multiplayer paths.',\n'Specify whether standalone multiplayer must cross NAT without manual signaling, and whether a WebGL fallback is desired.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('test.py');s=p.read_text();needle=\\\"        # Cooldown, flight handling, damage, failure and pickup systems.\\\"\ns=s.replace(needle,\\\"\\\"\\\"        page.get_by_role('button', name='About & credits').click()\n        credits = page.locator('#menu').inner_text()\n        check('Credits contain source and all feedback sections', all(title in credits for title in ['Source Information','Testing Feedback','Engine Feedback','Prompt Feedback','added on import']))\n        page.get_by_role('button', name='Library licenses').click()\n        check('Third-party licenses included', 'THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED' in page.locator('#menu').inner_text() and 'Apache License' in page.locator('#menu').inner_text())\n        page.get_by_role('button', name='Back to credits').click()\n        page.get_by_role('button', name='Back', exact=True).click()\n        check('Credits and licenses return to result screen', js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().screen') == 'result')\n        # Cooldown, flight handling, damage, failure and pickup systems.\\\"\\\"\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"check('Transport loss ends the sortie', js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().completed && \"'!__POSE__.game.won'\"'))\\\", \\\"check('Transport loss ends the sortie', js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().completed && \"'!__POSE__.game.won'\"'))\\\\n        js(page, '__POSE__.game.begin()')\\\\n        check('Fresh run clears prior victory and result state', not js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().won') and not js(page, '__POSE__.snapshot().completed'))\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nbiome check --write --linter-enabled=false --assist-enabled=false src/*.js build.mjs\nbiome format --write src/style.css\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# The Empire Strikes a Pose\n\nAn original, unofficial snow-battle flight comic inspired by the 1982 game. Three.js r180, WebGPU, Rapier 0.19.3. All art, animation, music, effects and gibberish voices are procedural. The root HTML embeds every runtime dependency and can be opened directly with \"'`file://`.\n\nThe deliverable is `../The-Empire-Strikes-a-Pose-Star-Wars-The-Empire-Strikes-Back-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-011138.html`. The exit interview is beside it and is also embedded into About & credits.\n\n## Play\n\nClear three scouts, use tow lines to topple two walkers, then escort Ark and defeat Blackfin. Keep within 145 metres of the transport. A full AI sortie takes about two minutes; a first human sortie is expected to take longer (human timing unknown).\n\n- Keyboard/mouse: WASD steer and throttle, mouse aims, left click fires, Shift boosts, S brakes, Space launches/releases a cable, Q changes target, C changes camera, Escape pauses. J also fires.\n- Standard gamepad: left stick steers and throttles; right stick aims; R2/RT fires; L2/LT boosts; R1/RB brakes; Cross/A tows; Square/X changes target; Triangle/Y changes camera; Options/Menu pauses. D-pad or stick navigates menus, Cross/A selects and Circle/B returns. Xbox labels are available in Settings.\n- Touch: invisible left drag steers/throttles; right drag aims/fires. Cannons assist automatically. A context-sensitive tow button appears beside walkers. Multitouch is supported.\n\nContinuous fire overheats the cannons. Cyan repair buoys restore hull and cool the weapons. While tethered, steer to change orbit radius; boost adds speed and tension. Two wraps topple a walker. The camera widens during cable flight.\n\nPause → Developer tools exposes live speed, turn rate, weapon damage, incoming damage, enemy pressure, wraps and simulation rate; plus reset, invulnerability, AI pilot, collision shapes, repair, frame step, spawn and chapter tools.\n\nTitle idle for ten seconds starts a looping, invulnerable AI demo. Any input returns to the title without launching a run.\n\n## Multiplayer\n\nAI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1–4 seats. Each player has their own world and competes by sortie score. Wing craft are visible in the same mission chapter but cannot collide. The unmodified session client is embedded first in the head. Session startup, seeding, progress, ghost state, time-up result, leave and end behavior follow the supplied contract.\n\nStandalone has same-origin BroadcastChannel rooms for up to four pilots, and a two-player serverless WebRTC invite/answer exchange. The direct link uses host ICE candidates without a public signaling or relay service; use a same-network or directly reachable connection. Internet NAT traversal is unknown. AI Hub manages internet sessions. The Wing link screen includes complete pairing instructions and error messages.\n\n## Build and test\n\nFrom this directory:\n\n```sh\nnpm install --ignore-scripts\nnpm run build\nnpm run --silent test\n```\n\nThe test command prints only failures and one count. It uses the installed Python Playwright environment and Chromium, starts its own loopback HTTP server on an OS-assigned port, verifies the served game identity, closes its own pages/browser and stops its own server. It saves JSON reports and visual-only captures in `test-artifacts/`.\n\nThe suite covers direct-file startup, embedded script parsing, versions, full combat/tow/escort/ace victory, heat, repair, failures, pause and live balance tools, gamepad stubs, touch contacts, attract looping, live/offline audio, both standalone transports, and the official Hub harness in normal, loss/jitter and host-departure cases. WebGPU canvas capture is blank in this headless setup; visual captures use the engine'\"'s WebGL backend. Actual hardware/controller/touch/TV and audible listening review remain unknown.\n\n\"'`?test=1` exposes deterministic simulation hooks on `window.__POSE__`; the normal page exposes only state and audio diagnostics. `?renderer=webgl` explicitly selects the built-in fallback. `?manual=1` disables the animation clock for test driving.\n\n## Extend the slice\n\n`src/mission.js` contains chapter titles, briefing lines, spawn positions, repair placements and default balance. `src/art.js` builds the world and animated machines. `src/game.js` owns simulation, physics and progression; `src/ui.js`, `src/audio.js` and `src/network.js` handle their respective systems. `build.mjs` embeds all code, metadata and third-party license texts into the root HTML. The original Hub client and harness are retained beside the sources.\n\nSource research: none. The explicitly requested AI Hub contract/client/harness and pinned package dependencies were downloaded without web searching. The random title draw used Python `secrets.randbelow(50)`; its result is recorded in `title-selection.json`.\nEOF\nnpm run build\nnpm run --silent test'","aggregated_output":"Checked 7 files in 28ms. Fixed 7 files.\nFormatted 1 file in 6ms. Fixed 1 file.\nnpm notice run build\nnpm notice run node build.mjs\nBuilt The-Empire-Strikes-a-Pose-Star-Wars-The-Empire-Strikes-Back-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-011138.html (2.95 MiB; all runtime dependencies embedded)\n68 checks: 68 passed, 0 failed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
